    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "1578d27733e018f783d2d013f66e98a809460dab",
            "parents": [
                "c088d1085c2069caa0ed50d9d6693a4aa3e99dd1"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/46/83946/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "createdOn": 1758616786,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't really seem like something that should be specific to one particular machine (ie. yv4).  It almost seems like something that should be done directly in the object mapper repository as a default behavior, or maybe done in meta-phosphor if they don't like it in the phosphor-objmgr repository.  Can you start a discussion on the mailing list about this potential problem?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the feedback! But I'm not quite sure where the mailing list for the `phosphor-objmgr` repository is located. Were you referring to starting a discussion by opening a new issue on GitHub instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There is only one openbmc mailing list.  openbmc@lists.ozlabs.org.\n\nPlease don't use Github issues for discussions; almost nobody monitors them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I\u2019ve sent the discussion email titled \u201c Resending (plain text): [DISCUSSION] Policy for handling ObjectMapper stop: reboot BMC and refuse manual stop\u201d to openbmc@lists.ozlabs.org. It\u2019s now visible in the archive: https://lists.ozlabs.org/pipermail/openbmc/2025-October/037480.html\n\nIn the meantime, before a community decision is made, would it be acceptable to keep this change applied at the platform layer?\n\nThanks for your guidance!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Lets remove this from meta-yosemite4 once we have a final home for it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not sure whether I need to execute a service via `ExecStopPost` before rebooting, to run `systemctl show xyz.openbmc_project.ObjectMapper` or create an event log for easier debugging."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "If we want to use `log-create` to generate an standard event log indicating that the `Object Mapper` has previously stopped, then we might need to define an appropriate interface in `phosphor-dbus-interface` to represent service states (such as Active or Stopped).\nSo far, I haven\u2019t seen an existing interface that serves this purpose. `Software` interfaces in `phosphor-dbus-interface` seem to be related to image updates in the software stack."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "If we want to use log-create to generate an event log indicating that the Object Mapper has previously stopped, then we should define an appropriate interface in phosphor-dbus-interface to represent service states (such as Active or Stopped). So far, I haven\u2019t seen an existing interface that serves this purpose. Most of the interfaces in phosphor-dbus-interface seem to be related to image updates in the software stack."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Unintentionally added a redundant comment."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "If the `Object Mapper` is restarted during runtime and a service tries to access information while the data is incomplete, based on my experience, it can lead to the following issues:\n(1) `pldmd` may use `GetSubtree` to retrieve MCTP EID information and mistakenly assume that the EID does not exist, resulting in the removal of the corresponding sensor object and stopping sensor polling.\n(2)`phosphor-state-manager` may fail to retrieve the correct `PowerRestorePolicy` during system state discovery, which prevents it from initiating a host power-on operation.\n\nBasically, any operation that relies on `GetSubtree` to fetch D-Bus information can be affected."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't seem lik"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pete O_o",
                        "email": "pmb@meta.com",
                        "username": "waffle2k"
                    },
                    "message": "Let's do this until the move to get it landed in the general case is complete"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "LGTM. Lets get this in and soak it in Y4 while we get community consensus on where its final resting place should be. @eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com please continue driving it on the mailing list."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
