            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Why block the manual start/stop?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Currently, it's hard to determine from the journal whether the user actually performed a manual stop. However, this operation can cause the BMC to enter a problematic error state, so we may consider making this restriction an optional feature."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "stumbled upon this change, trying to understand it now.\n\nWon't the mapper enter the same failure state again?\n\nWill it not cause reboot loop in worst case, making the BMC unreachable via ssh?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Indeed, the current approach can lead to such situations, so we\u2019re also moving toward making it configurable as an option. Additionally, Patrick mentioned that `phosphor-systemd-target-monitor` can be used to collect a BMC crashdump when critical services fail. I\u2019ll look into the related functionality to see how we can leverage it to achieve these goals."
                }
            ],
